data: [{"tag":"search_results_json","payload":"{\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Hello, world - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hello,_world\",\"snippet\":\"&quot;Time to hello world&quot; (TTHW) is the time it takes to author a &quot;Hello, world&quot; program in a given programming language. This is one measure of a programming language&#39;s ease of use.\",\"rank\":1,\"source\":\"en.wikipedia.org\"},{\"title\":\"Hello World (film) - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hello_World_(film)\",\"snippet\":\"Hello World premiered in Kyoto on September 11, 2019, and was released in Japan on September 20. The film grossed over $25 million worldwide, with critics praising the direction and animation. The film received novelization, two manga adaptations, and an anime spin-off.\",\"rank\":2,\"source\":\"en.wikipedia.org\"},{\"title\":\"Hello World - Simple source code examples\",\"url\":\"https://www.helloworld.org/\",\"snippet\":\"Hello World. A &quot;Hello world&quot; program is a computer program that outputs &quot;Hello World&quot; (or some variant) on a display device. The first known version of this program comes from Brian Kernighan&#39;s paper A Tutorial Introduction to the Language B from 1972 (chapter 7). In it&#39;s first form it was used to show how to use external variables in B but since then it has become pretty much the standard example to show the very basic syntax and most simple program in.\",\"rank\":3,\"source\":\"helloworld.org\"},{\"title\":\"Hello, world! | Hello, World!\",\"url\":\"https://web.archive.org/web/20150227155541/http://hello-world.io/hello-world/\",\"snippet\":\"This news instantly put me into dad-mode, and I knew that it was time to go back to the “real world” to get a job with a good salary and benefits. I ended up with one of the most amazing companies a person could ask to work for, and they offered the ideal package. A great salary, great benefits, trips to Vegas and New York City, a great group of pe..\",\"rank\":4,\"source\":\"web.archive.org\"},{\"title\":\"robsheldon.com: Hello, world.\",\"url\":\"https://web.archive.org/web/20120219115509/http://robsheldon.com/sopa-pipa\",\"snippet\":\"Naturally, they turn to resourceful groups during campaign time, and there is an unspoken and unwritten mutual understanding that, in return for the groups&#39; campaign season support, politicians will pass some laws which will benefit the groups -- even at the expense of the voting citizenry who are actually responsible for (often reluctantly) keepin..\",\"rank\":5,\"source\":\"web.archive.org\"}],\"answer_box\":null}","sent_at":0,"kagi_version":"202609101459.stage.d843693"}]

